From: Adam Hillson <598804+BadAd84@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] glm index: TF_GLM_OVN_INDEX_REGROUP, the reduce-scatter head sum

ai-engine 5da368af1 grafted onto 0009 (INDEX_SCHED). Prompt launches take
tf_glm_index_scores_regroup (glm_index_regroup.cuh, included from glm_index.cu so the
symbol is compiled into the image): 7 shuffles a group, every lane stores its column, no
stage buffer, full unroll. Each column's sum keeps INDEX_SCHED's operand pairs. The pk8
scorer arm is left out: PK8 is its own knob, ported separately, so Scorer keeps
plain/sched/regroup only. Production: -4.2..-5.2% on the scoring kernel; GPU check
glm-index-regroup-check rides in the patch; 3 host mutants killed at the source.

Gates on pin+0001..0010: check-native-cuda-host green, whole-tree fmt green, lean
base-vs-head 0 new, fatbins green with glm_index_regroup.cuh in the include list.

Folded in by the 2026-11-12 fold (work/fold/MAP.tsv), each hunk where it belongs:
- 0056: glm-index-regroup-check is registered, and the inputs it reads are pub

Re-seated on v1.2.7 (93a2e93ecebff8aa52b88e58c5dd222516e69c5f, from pin 9c9bf542) by the 2026-11-12 re-seat (work/reseat/DECISIONS.md):
- lean_check.py's DIRECT_GETENV/HIDDEN_GETENV: every TF_* setting this patch reads is a row of platform/environment.zig with a line in docs/environment.md, read through cuda.ovn or environment, never getenv. Row: TF_GLM_OVN_INDEX_REGROUP (flag).
- cuda_index.zig: the Scorer enum and its test land above index-decode-windows' registry form of decodeFrom.
- glm-index-regroup-check joins glm_ovn_checks.zig.
- source: work/fold/0014-index-regroup.patch

